{"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "dword", "ucas": "dsq(x: f32 in 1..2, y: f32 in 3..4) = f32(f64(x) * f64(x) - f64(y) * f64(y))\ndword dsq", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "dword", "model": "gt1030", "check_points": 4096, "check_max_rel": 7.6094437125407e-15, "rewritten": true, "cost_f64": 73.75, "cost_form": 13, "bound_relative": 2.2026827222644014e-14, "bound_absolute": 1.9539927245123908e-13, "form": "pairs", "body": "t1 + (x*x - t2 - (y*y + (t1 - t2)) + (fma(x, x, -x*x) - fma(y, y, -y*y))) where t1 = x*x - y*y, t2 = t1 + y*y", "defined": "dsq_dw"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "derivation", "text": "the standard model of rounding and the error-free transformations, composed over the parameters' ranges"}, "files": [], "text": "dword dsq under gt1030: the f64 arithmetic over f32 (u = 2^-24, u64 = 2^-53)\n  as written  cost 73.75   error against the exact value <= 3.997e-16 (3.6 u64) relative\n  f32 alone   cost 2       error <= 2.146e-07 (3.6 u) relative: as f32 within 0.5 + 3.6 ulp\n  f32 pairs   cost 13      error <= 2.203e-14 (6.2 u^2) relative: as f32 within 0.5 + 3.7e-07 ulp\n  required: the result feeds an f32: within 0.5 + 2^-10 ulp of the exact value (ten guard bits; `ulp X`, `tol R` or `atol T` to change)\n  -> f32 pairs: cost 13 against 73.75 (-82.4%), 15 f32 operations for 6\n  the form:\n    t1 = x * x                               !\n    t2 = y * y                               !\n    t3 = t1 - t2                             !\n    t4 = -t1\n    t5 = fma(x, x, t4)                       !\n    t6 = -t2\n    t7 = fma(y, y, t6)                       !\n    t8 = t3 + t2                             !\n    t9 = t3 - t8                             !\n    t10 = t1 - t8                            !\n    t11 = t2 + t9                            !\n    t12 = t10 - t11                          !\n    t13 = t5 - t7\n    t14 = t12 + t13\n    t15 = t3 + t14                           !\n    result: t15\n    ! 11 operations of the error-free transformations: exact only as written, so they are\n      NoContraction in SPIR-V, `precise` in GLSL (no fused multiply-add, no reassociation)\n  each value: its range, the derived error bound, the algorithm:\n      f64(x)*f64(x)                            [1, 4]                   0 u^2          2Prod (exact)\n      f64(y)*f64(y)                            [9, 16]                  0 u^2          2Prod (exact)\n      f64(x)*f64(x) - f64(y)*f64(y)            [-15, -5]                6.2 u^2        SloppyDWPlusDW\n  derivation (u = 2^-24; RN rounds to nearest; a pair x~ = xh + xl has |xl| <= u |xh|):\n    2Sum(a, b): s = RN(a + b), a' = RN(s - b), b' = RN(s - a'), t = RN((a - a') + (b - b')):\n      s + t = a + b exactly (Knuth), |t| <= u |s|\n    Fast2Sum(a, b): s = RN(a + b), t = RN(b - RN(s - a)): s + t = a + b exactly when |a| >= |b| (Dekker)\n    2Prod(a, b): p = RN(a b), e = fma(a, b, -p): p + e = a b exactly while |a b| >= 2^-102\n      (a b - p is a multiple of ulp(a) ulp(b) below ulp(p): representable), |e| <= u |a b|\n    SloppyDWPlusDW(x~, y~): (sh, sl) = 2Sum(xh, yh); v = RN(xl + yl); w = RN(sl + v);\n      (zh, zl) = Fast2Sum(sh, w): zh + zl = x~ + y~ + d1 (xl + yl) + d2 (sl + v): at most\n      u (u A) + u (u |sh| + (1 + u) u A), A = |xh| + |yh|: 3.000 u^2 |x~ + y~| at kappa = 1,\n      (1 + 2 kappa) u^2 in general, kappa = (|x| + |y|) / |x + y| the largest on the ranges\n    composition: a product's errors multiply (1 + ex)(1 + ey)(1 + e) - 1, a quotient's (1 + ex)(1 + e) / (1 - ey) - 1,\n      a sum's are kappa max(ex, ey) + e (1 + kappa max(ex, ey)), a square root halves its operand's\n  conditions:\n    finite inputs (an infinity or a NaN gives NaN where f64 would carry it)\n    no overflow: the largest value is 16, below 2^127 (derived from the ranges)\n    no underflow: the 2 error-free products stay above 2^-102 (derived from the ranges)\n    Fast2Sum's precondition |a| >= |b|: derived in each use from the magnitudes above\n  check (sampled, not a proof): 4096 points of the domain, the largest error against the exact value\n    (long double) 2.1 u^2 (the bound: 6.2); the f64 program's 0 u64\n  defined dsq_dw: the form as a function (cost dsq_dw, error dsq_dw ~ dsq)\n"}
