{"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "dword", "ucas": "dword dsq ulp 4", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "dword", "model": "gt1030", "check_points": 4096, "check_max_rel": 1.4512724887964372e-07, "rewritten": true, "cost_f64": 73.75, "cost_form": 2, "bound_relative": 2.1457673042860283e-07, "bound_absolute": 2.086162638192946e-06, "form": "f32", "body": "x*x - y*y", "defined": "dsq_dw"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "derivation", "text": "the standard model of rounding and the error-free transformations, composed over the parameters' ranges"}, "files": [], "text": "dword dsq under gt1030: the f64 arithmetic over f32 (u = 2^-24, u64 = 2^-53)\n  as written  cost 73.75   error against the exact value <= 3.997e-16 (3.6 u64) relative\n  f32 alone   cost 2       error <= 2.146e-07 (3.6 u) relative: as f32 within 0.5 + 3.6 ulp\n  f32 pairs   cost 13      error <= 2.203e-14 (6.2 u^2) relative: as f32 within 0.5 + 3.7e-07 ulp\n  required: the f32 result within 0.5 + 4 ulp of the exact value (ulp)\n  -> f32 alone: cost 2 against 73.75 (-97.3%), 3 f32 operations for 6\n  the form:\n    t1 = x * x\n    t2 = y * y\n    t3 = t1 - t2\n    result: t3\n  each value: its range, the derived error bound, the algorithm:\n      f64(x)*f64(x)                            [1, 4]                   1 u            one f32 multiply\n      f64(y)*f64(y)                            [9, 16]                  1 u            one f32 multiply\n      f64(x)*f64(x) - f64(y)*f64(y)            [-15, -5]                3.6 u          one f32 add\n  conditions:\n    finite inputs (an infinity or a NaN gives NaN where f64 would carry it)\n    no overflow: the largest value is 16, below 2^127 (derived from the ranges)\n  check (sampled, not a proof): 4096 points of the domain, the largest error against the exact value\n    (long double) 2.4 u (the bound: 3.6); the f64 program's 0 u64\n  defined dsq_dw: the form as a function (cost dsq_dw, error dsq_dw ~ dsq)\n"}
{"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "cost", "ucas": "q(x: f32 in 0.5..8) = f32(f16(x)) * 2\ncost q", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "cost", "model": "gt1030", "total": 1, "operations": 1, "by_class": [{"class": "fmul", "count": 1, "each": 1, "cost": 1}], "driver_folds": [{"round_trip": "f32 -> f16 -> f32", "expression": "f32(f16(x))", "relies_on_rounding": true, "witness": "x=0.717493892: the program expects 0.717285156, the folded one gives 0.717493892"}], "selects": [], "best_total": 1}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "cost of q under gt1030: 1 (1 operations, shared subterms counted once)\n  fmul             1 x 1     = 1\n  the driver folds f32 -> f16 -> f32 (model gt1030): f32(f16(x)) is priced 0 and computes x itself\n      warning: q relies on that rounding (quantisation): at x=0.717493892: the program expects 0.717285156, the folded one gives 0.717493892\n      `foldproof q` gives the rounding in a form no float fold reaches\n"}
{"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "foldproof", "ucas": "foldproof q", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "foldproof", "model": "gt1030", "round_trips": 1, "folded": 1, "round_trip_forms": [{"round_trip": "f32(f16(x))", "relies_on_rounding": true, "check_patterns": 726, "check_differences": 0, "form": "asfloat(asuint(x) + 4095 + (asuint(x) >> 13 & 1) & 0xffffe000)", "full": false, "cost": 6, "proved": true}], "rewritten": true, "defined": "q_fp", "body": "2asfloat(asuint(x) + 4095 + (asuint(x) >> 13 & 1) & 0xffffe000)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "foldproof q under gt1030: 1 conversion round trip the driver folds\n  f32(f16(x)), its operand in [0.5, 8]: gt1030 folds f32 -> f16 -> f32, so the card computes the operand itself\n    the program relies on the rounding: at x=0.717493892: the program expects 0.717285156, the folded one gives 0.717493892\n    fold-proof: asfloat(asuint(x) + 4095 + (asuint(x) >> 13 & 1) & 0xffffe000)\n      cost 6 under gt1030 (the round trip as written would be 6; folded it is 0 and does not round)\n    proof:\n      1. between 2^-14 and 2^16 the f16 values of a binade are the f32 values whose 13 low mantissa\n         bits are 0; the bit pattern grows with |x| and a carry out of the mantissa is the next\n         binade's first value, so rounding the value to f16 (nearest, ties to even) is rounding\n         the pattern to a multiple of 2^13 (nearest, ties to the even quotient)\n      2. (b + 4095 + (b >> 13 & 1)) & ~8191 is that rounding of b, for every 32-bit b: against\n         q = b >> 13, r = b mod 2^13, (q + (r > 2^12 or r = 2^12 and q odd)) << 13: proved by SAT (both sides bit-blasted)\n      3. the range: every operand is 0 or has 2^-14 <= |x| < 65520, so no result is subnormal or\n         infinite and the carry never reaches the sign bit\n    check (not the proof): 726 bit patterns, both signs, exponent fields 126..130, ties and their\n      neighbours at every mantissa bit: all equal to the evaluator's round trip\n  defined q_fp = 2asfloat(asuint(x) + 4095 + (asuint(x) >> 13 & 1) & 0xffffe000)\n  cost under gt1030: 7 (as written, folded: 1)\n"}
